          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Is sharing a splitter with neighbors a good idea?</h3>

          <p>
            It can be. Two or three households can split the cost of one gas machine and take turns, provided everyone agrees up front on who handles maintenance and where it is stored. However you get access to one, build the job around the right tools: a good <a href="/best-chainsaw/">chainsaw</a> to cut rounds, a splitter, and a hookaroon to move pieces turn a brutal chore into a manageable one. For tidying the yard around the woodpile, see our <a href="/best-weed-eater/">weed eater guide</a>.
          </p>
